text:
Separate projects in their code, but the Composer still carries HPSM's name and lives in HPSM's places. Measured just now:

1. HPSM (the HP SOW work): its own folder, code repo datasecau/HPSM, records repo datasecau/HPSM-analysis, Jira HPSM. Readiness only, no build.

2. HPSM-POC (the Playbook POC under its own SOW): its own folder, repos datasecau/HPSM-POC and HPSM-POC-analysis, Jira HPSMPOC. Separate throughout.

3. Security Composer (internal Datasec): its own folder since 24 Sep, but conflated in four places:
- its code repo is named datasecau/HPSM-light;
- an older clone of that repo still sits inside the HPSM folder (6_Policy_Composer), where the Composer started on 10 Sep;
- its demo VM is called hpsm-composer-demo and runs in HPSM's Azure resource group (hpsm-dev-rg);
- HPSM's credentials folder holds a file pointing at the Composer demo.

That is why I mixed them up this morning; my mistake.

Recommendation: separate the Composer properly. Rename the repo (GitHub keeps the old name working as a redirect), move the stale clone out of the HPSM folder, and give the Composer demo its own resource group and name the next time it is rebuilt. I'll put that on a card with the cost and steps. Nothing changes until you choose.
